### Scenario 1 - Auto approve under $100

POST http://localhost:7071/api/expenses/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Jingjing Duan",
  "employeeEmail": "test@example.com",
  "amount": 50,
  "category": "meals",
  "description": "Team lunch",
  "managerEmail": "manager@example.com"
}

### Expense requires manager

POST http://localhost:7071/api/expenses/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Jingjing Duan",
  "employeeEmail": "test@example.com",
  "amount": 250,
  "category": "equipment",
  "description": "New monitor",
  "managerEmail": "manager@example.com"
}


### Scenario 2 - Manager approval required

POST http://localhost:7071/api/expenses/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Jingjing Duan",
  "employeeEmail": "test@example.com",
  "amount": 250,
  "category": "equipment",
  "description": "New monitor",
  "managerEmail": "manager@example.com"
}

### Manager approves

POST http://localhost:7071/api/expenses/5a978623963547cfb2608699d81ce509/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "approve"
}


### Scenario 3 - Manager rejects

POST http://localhost:7071/api/expenses/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Jingjing Duan",
  "employeeEmail": "test@example.com",
  "amount": 250,
  "category": "equipment",
  "description": "New monitor",
  "managerEmail": "manager@example.com"
}

### Manager approves
POST http://localhost:7071/api/expenses/eaf7732891424e4094e711e988a01631/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "reject"
}